diff --git a/.changeset/preencoded-reference-continuity.md b/.changeset/preencoded-reference-continuity.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..d267a689
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/preencoded-reference-continuity.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+---
+webrtc-sys: patch
+libwebrtc: patch
+livekit: patch
+livekit-ffi: patch
+---
+
+Fence pre-encoded reference continuity across WebRTC encoder-queue drops.
+The pass-through encoder requests a fresh keyframe and suppresses dependent
+access units until it arrives, instead of forwarding a damaged reference chain.
+Continuity is private to each encoder and resets on encoder/source replacement.
diff --git a/.changeset/reused-screen-sender.md b/.changeset/reused-screen-sender.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..5896d522
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/reused-screen-sender.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+---
+livekit: patch
+libwebrtc: patch
+webrtc-sys: patch
+livekit-ffi: patch
+---
+
+Keep the current track ID in publisher SDP when reusing an RTP sender for a
+replacement screen track. Return an absent track safely for inactive senders.
+This preserves bounded transceiver reuse while allowing the SFU to associate
+new RTP media with the replacement publication.
